  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-008">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-008</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>Verification Triad: Deterministic Pytest Suites vs. LLM-as-a-Judge</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-008</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Relying solely on LLM judges misses subtle logic defects, whereas mandatory deterministic test execution eliminates silent logic regressions.</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-009">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-009</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>AST Subgraphs vs. Raw Grep</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-009</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>2-hop Tree-sitter AST neighborhood extraction reduces prompt context size while increasing first-pass code generation accuracy.</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-010">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-010</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>Predictable Cloud-Native Execution: Strict 512Mi Memory Clamping</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-010</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Explicit cgroup memory limits (`512Mi` compilation profile, `30Mi` micro-sandbox) prevent noisy-neighbor OOM exhaustion on host nodes.</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-011">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-011</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>Autonomous Security Remediation at Scale</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-011</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Separating meta-orchestration, credentialed factory controls, and surgical code-fix loops enables automated CVE remediation with sharp LLM token savings across the historical 69-repo portfolio (`64` public = `22` original + `42` maintained forks, plus `5` private/archived). A...</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ2" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ2" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-012">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-012</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>Supply Chain Upgrade Paradox Across Fleet &amp; Cluster</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-012</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Synchronized lockfile exports and hash-pinned transitives prevent secondary vulnerabilities introduced by naive package bumps while reducing active Trivy cluster findings (`429 -&gt; 396` CRITICAL, `3,660 -&gt; 2,973` HIGH, `720` fixed).</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-013">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-013</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>End-to-End Autonomous Mission &amp; Hatchet-Orchestrated R2R GraphRAG (`Mission #476`)</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-013</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Post-merge-only R2R v3 GraphRAG ingestion orchestrated via Hatchet produces zero duplicate ingestions, reliable Leiden community graphs, and grounded MCP retrieval.</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ2" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ2" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/EXP-2026-014">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#Experiment" />
    <dg:nodeId>EXP-2026-014</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>Parallel Autonomous Swarm Mode &amp; Contention-Free R2R GraphRAG (`Mission #478`)</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>verified</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/notebooks.html#exp-2026-014</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Parallel `[P]` execution across isolated gVisor lanes with `fan-in-synthesize` and read/write-split `r2r-reader` RO replicas increases throughput without Postgres/pgvector lock contention.</dg:summary>
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:MEASURES rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1" />
    <dg:VALIDATES_HYPOTHESIS rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#ResearchHypothesis" />
    <dg:nodeId>RQ1</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>RQ1: Can autonomous agents safely reduce Mean Time to Recovery (`MTTR`) under strict HITL gates?</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>experimental</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/RESEARCH.md#rq1</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Contract-driven agent pipelines backed by durable Hatchet checkpoints, R2R GraphRAG context, and Review Guidance loops reduce remediation cycle time and MTTR without sacrificing CI verification or Vertex 4 human approval.</dg:summary>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#ResearchHypothesis" />
    <dg:nodeId>RQ2</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>RQ2: Can cryptographic Non-Human Identities (NHI) and Verifiable Credentials improve governance and traceability?</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>experimental</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/RESEARCH.md#rq2</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Binding agent missions to Ed25519 W3C Verifiable Credentials (`Ed25519Signature2020`), 300 s Vault JIT tokens (`54.2 ns` `ZeroizeOnDrop`), LiteLLM `X-Vtag-*` FinOps headers, and causal Semantica lineage yields tamper-evident attribution across multi-repo PRs.</dg:summary>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#ResearchHypothesis" />
    <dg:nodeId>RQ3</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>RQ3: Can declarative GitOps, admission policies, and kernel sandboxing act as an enforceable security boundary?</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>experimental</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/RESEARCH.md#rq3</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Combining FluxCD v2 declarative reconciliation, OpenZiti mTLS 1.3, default-deny NetworkPolicies, `ValidatingAdmissionPolicy` resource clamps (`&lt;= 30 Mi` / `250m` micro-sandbox, `&lt;= 512 Mi` / `500m` compilation), and `gVisor (runsc)` prevents privilege escalation and fleet reg...</dg:summary>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lgcorzo.github.io/kg/RQ4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://lgcorzo.github.io/ontology/dark-gravity#ResearchHypothesis" />
    <dg:nodeId>RQ4</dg:nodeId>
    <rdfs:label>RQ4: Can structured, AST- and GraphRAG-grounded agentic workflows outperform ad-hoc workflows on reliability and token efficiency?</rdfs:label>
    <dg:verificationStatus>experimental</dg:verificationStatus>
    <dg:canonicalUrl>https://lgcorzo.github.io/RESEARCH.md#rq4</dg:canonicalUrl>
    <dg:summary>Pairing AST neighborhood extraction (`OSR &lt; 5%`), deterministic test verification (replacing pure LLM judges), R2R Leiden GraphRAG with `r2r-reader` RO replicas, and parallel Swarm `[P]` execution yields higher first-pass accuracy and lower token overhead per merged PR.</dg:summary>
  </rdf:Description>
